  "steps": [
    "Blanch spinach in hot water for 4–5 minutes and immediately transfer to ice-cold water to retain its vibrant green colour.",
    "Boil soya chunks with bay leaf, black cardamom, cloves, ginger-garlic paste, salt and a pinch of sugar for 6–7 minutes. Drain and squeeze out excess water.",
    "Blend blanched spinach, green chillies, garlic, paneer and a little water into a smooth paste.",
    "Heat a little oil in a pan. Add chopped onion and garlic and sauté for 3–4 minutes.",
    "Add turmeric, coriander powder and red chilli powder. Cook for 2–3 minutes.",
    "Add the palak paste and salt. Mix well and cook for 4–5 minutes.",
    "Add boiled soya chunks and cook for another 5–7 minutes.",
    "Finish with garam masala and cook for 4–5 minutes.",
    "Top with low-fat cream and chilli oil (optional).",
    "Serve hot with roti or rice!"
  ],
